00:43:48.860 --> 00:43:50.020
That's not all of our calling.

00:43:50.100 --> 00:43:51.920
We aren't meant to be carbon copies of him

00:43:51.920 --> 00:43:53.280
or of one another or anybody else.

00:43:53.780 --> 00:43:55.940
God has a unique calling for each one of us.

00:43:56.500 --> 00:43:58.820
What might your unique calling be?

00:43:58.940 --> 00:44:00.720
Who is God calling you to become?

00:44:01.320 --> 00:44:02.880
And even as we reflect on Paul's story,

00:44:02.940 --> 00:44:04.620
it might cause us to think about that

00:44:04.620 --> 00:44:06.940
because we see the importance

00:44:06.940 --> 00:44:08.600
of different people along the way.

00:44:09.320 --> 00:44:10.620
Like, have you thought about this?

00:44:10.980 --> 00:44:13.760
Paul wouldn't be Paul without his parents who raised him.

00:44:15.100 --> 00:44:16.240
Some of you here in this room,

00:44:16.300 --> 00:44:17.720
you're parents, you're raising your kids,

00:44:17.800 --> 00:44:19.760
you're like, man, I'm changing the diapers.

00:44:20.460 --> 00:44:21.520
I'm just chasing him around the house.

00:44:21.580 --> 00:44:22.420
I'm trying to clean him up.

00:44:22.480 --> 00:44:24.440
I'm trying to help him get ready for school,

00:44:24.540 --> 00:44:25.960
trying to help with the last minute project.

00:44:26.140 --> 00:44:27.040
Oh my gosh.

00:44:27.880 --> 00:44:29.940
Can you realize God has a purpose for you

00:44:29.940 --> 00:44:31.140
in that role as a parent?

00:44:32.000 --> 00:44:34.240
Have you thought about that Paul wouldn't be Paul

00:44:34.240 --> 00:44:36.120
without Gamaliel who taught him?

00:44:36.960 --> 00:44:38.320
Some of you have a heart to teach,

00:44:38.320 --> 00:44:39.740
to invest in the next generation.

00:44:40.120 --> 00:44:41.020
That's so huge.

00:44:41.500 --> 00:44:42.160
That's valuable.

00:44:42.320 --> 00:44:42.880
That's important.

00:44:43.640 --> 00:44:45.120
Paul wouldn't be Paul without Stephen,

00:44:45.980 --> 00:44:48.200
the guy who testified in the streets of Jerusalem

00:44:48.200 --> 00:44:50.180
and even at the threat to his own life

00:44:50.180 --> 00:44:51.240
wouldn't back down.

00:44:51.780 --> 00:44:53.640
That Paul not only condemned him to death

00:44:53.640 --> 00:44:54.820
but sat and watched him

00:44:54.820 --> 00:44:56.500
as he died for his faith in Christ.

00:44:56.840 --> 00:44:58.980
Paul wouldn't be Paul without seeing that.

00:44:59.860 --> 00:45:01.360
Paul wouldn't be Paul without Ananias

00:45:01.360 --> 00:45:03.920
who came to Paul at a moment of crisis

00:45:03.920 --> 00:45:06.680
and prayed for him to receive his sight.

00:45:06.680 --> 00:45:09.800
Paul wouldn't be Paul without Ananias coming and praying for him

00:45:09.800 --> 00:45:11.260
Paul wouldn't be Paul without Barnabas

00:45:11.260 --> 00:45:13.460
coming and taking him under his wing

00:45:13.460 --> 00:45:15.140
mentoring him, encouraging him

00:45:15.140 --> 00:45:16.820
Paul wouldn't be Paul without Timothy

00:45:16.820 --> 00:45:19.820
the apprentice who came after him

00:45:19.820 --> 00:45:21.240
and continued his ministry

00:45:21.240 --> 00:45:23.720
each of us here has our own

00:45:23.720 --> 00:45:25.620
calling that's valuable in the kingdom

00:45:25.620 --> 00:45:27.780
of God and as we pray about that

00:45:27.780 --> 00:45:29.660
explore that, discover that this coming year

00:45:29.660 --> 00:45:32.040
I believe that God will lead us to take bold steps of faith

00:45:32.040 --> 00:45:33.660
together in our church family

00:45:33.660 --> 00:45:35.520
and see what it is that God will do

00:45:35.980 --> 00:45:37.780
As we wrap up our time here today,

00:45:38.520 --> 00:45:39.660
what I want to point out

00:45:39.660 --> 00:45:42.500
is that all of this started for Paul.

00:45:42.640 --> 00:45:46.580
The pivot point was when he met Jesus for himself.

00:45:47.640 --> 00:45:48.740
And I think it's really appropriate

00:45:48.740 --> 00:45:49.900
that as we finish this time,

00:45:50.140 --> 00:45:51.380
as we respond to the Lord,

00:45:51.640 --> 00:45:53.540
that we actually do so by taking communion together

00:45:53.540 --> 00:45:55.180
and remembering Christ

00:45:55.180 --> 00:45:57.600
and remembering what he's done in our lives.

00:45:58.080 --> 00:45:58.600
And so if you will,

00:45:58.640 --> 00:46:00.300
can we take a moment and bow our heads together

00:46:00.300 --> 00:46:02.300
and we'll prepare to take communion in this moment?
